comments[1]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-11-09T08:31:50.013Z","harness:codex","Duplicate check: full strict all-status corpus plus keyword AND search for advisory feeds unavailable registry timeout OSV found only closed pm-eqxjzl. This is a diagnostic follow-up, not a reopened advisory implementation or permission to pass unavailable evidence."
notes[1]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-11-15T04:04:46.606Z","harness:claude-code","Recurrence 2026-11-15 around 03:20Z, during local merge verification of PR #1732: the WAN uplink was saturated (ping RTT 1.2-2.7 s, TCP connect 3-14 s), so pnpm audit exceeded the collector's 60 s bound and OSV querybatch the 15 s per-batch bound. The receipt again recorded only status unavailable for both feeds, with no reason code, so telling a slow-but-reachable network from an outage took manual curl and ping probes. Because repository-static-quality also declares repository-dependency-advisories-required, the advisory verdict blocked the whole static assurance gate, and the merge proceeded on pinned evidence instead (lockfile identical to main, 0 Dependabot alerts, a hosted pass on the same lockfile). A bounded reason code (connect_timeout vs deadline_exceeded vs http_status) would have made that call immediate. Related: pm-amy32s (local merge evidence)."
body: ""
